      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In coronary patients with \"relatively normal\" lipid values and hyperhomocystinemia (levels > or =15 micromol/L), significant 12% reductions in homocysteine levels occurred after cardiac rehabilitation and exercise training. This benefit from cardiac rehabilitation and exercise training may lead to 20% to 30% reductions in overall coronary artery disease risk."},
